::heading level=1 id=dev
The development harness
::end

::paragraph id=dev-intro
One command proves this repository: `dx run dev.dx`. Every gate below is a run block whose verdict is recorded in this document — a claim here is a thing the engine measured, never a thing a session remembered. Each gate declares the tree it judges (`reads=rust`, `reads=editor`, `reads=examples`), so editing any source file stales exactly the gates that read it, and the next plain run — or an agent's next read — re-proves them by itself. `dx run dev.dx --force` re-runs everything regardless, which is the honest move after changing anything the gates cannot see, like this machine's toolchains.
::end

