::paragraph id=paragraph-21
The `.dx-sync` gate checks whether substantial code changes land without a matching document change. It diffs the working tree against its merge-base with the default branch (falling back to reporting nothing to compare, on the default branch itself), then counts files and lines changed outside `.dx` paths against the same for `.dx` paths. If the non-`.dx` change is large — **3 or more files, or 150 or more inserted lines** — and the `.dx` side is untouched or touched by nothing bigger than pointer bumps (a pointer swap is always a fixed, tiny diff no matter how much content changed behind it, so a bumped pointer must not read as "it was documented"), the gate prints a loud warning naming the counts. This is a best-effort heuristic, never a blocker: it always exits 0, because a false positive on a refactor or a test-only change is expected and must never fail a real commit.
::end

::code id=dx-sync lang=bash run reads=CLAUDE.md,LICENSE,README.md,dev.dx,docs,editor,examples,index.dx,packaging,reports.dx,rust,validation.dx
# Determine the base commit for comparison
base=""
if git rev-parse origin/main >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  base=$(git merge-base origin/main HEAD)
elif git rev-parse master >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  base=$(git merge-base master HEAD)
fi

# If on default branch with no upstream divergence, nothing to check
if [ -z "$base" ] || [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "$base" ]; then
  echo "ok - nothing to compare"
  exit 0
fi

# Get the stat diff
diff_stat=$(git diff --stat "$base" HEAD 2>/dev/null)

# Count files and lines outside .dx paths, and the same for .dx paths
non_dx_count=$(echo "$diff_stat" | grep -v '\.dx ' | grep -c '|' || true)
non_dx_lines=$(echo "$diff_stat" | grep -v '\.dx ' | awk -F'|' '{sum += $2} END {print sum+0}')
dx_file_count=$(echo "$diff_stat" | grep -c '\.dx ' || true)
dx_lines=$(echo "$diff_stat" | grep '\.dx ' | awk -F'|' '{sum += $2} END {print sum+0}')

# Thresholds: 3+ non-.dx files OR 150+ lines outside .dx paths. The .dx side must be
# either untouched, or touched by nothing more than pointer bumps — a pointer swap is
# always a tiny, fixed-size diff (one line replaced) regardless of how much content
# actually changed behind it, so "the pointer moved" must not read as "it was documented".
if ([ "$non_dx_count" -ge 3 ] || [ "$non_dx_lines" -ge 150 ]) && [ "$dx_lines" -le $((dx_file_count * 3)) ]; then
  echo "warning: real code changes with no matching document change"
  echo "  non-.dx files changed: $non_dx_count, lines: $non_dx_lines"
  echo "  .dx files touched: $dx_file_count, lines: $dx_lines (pointer-bump-sized or less)"
  echo "  consider whether this work should be reflected in a document"
  # Continue without exit 1 - a suggestion, never a blocker; false positives are expected.
fi

echo "ok - .dx-sync gate: checked $non_dx_count non-.dx files ($non_dx_lines lines) against $dx_file_count .dx docs ($dx_lines lines)"
::end

